    requirement: "PROCEDURE PopulateGrid(Plaintext : STRING), using the global 2D array Grid[1:5,1:5]",
    prompt: [
      "A Caesar box cipher uses a grid of five rows and five columns. The padded plain",
      "text is exactly 25 characters; it is put into the grid row by row. The global 2D",
      "array `Grid` of type `CHAR` stores the characters.",
      "",
      "A procedure `PopulateGrid()` is called with the correctly padded plain text. It:",
      "- populates `Grid` from the plain text, filling row 1 first, then row 2, and so on",
      "- outputs the contents of `Grid` so that it is displayed row by row",
      "",
      "Write pseudocode for `PopulateGrid()`. Assume that `Grid` is global."
    ].join("\n"),
    model: `PROCEDURE PopulateGrid(Plaintext : STRING)
    DECLARE Row : INTEGER
    DECLARE Column : INTEGER
    DECLARE Index : INTEGER
    DECLARE RowString : STRING
    FOR Row <- 1 TO 5
        RowString <- ""
        FOR Column <- 1 TO 5
            Index <- (Row - 1) * 5 + Column
            Grid[Row, Column] <- MID(Plaintext, Index, 1)
            RowString <- RowString & MID(Plaintext, Index, 1)
        NEXT Column
        OUTPUT RowString
    NEXT Row
ENDPROCEDURE`,
