    chapter: "Ch11 Programming",
    requirement: "FUNCTION CheckNumber(Number : INTEGER) RETURNS BOOLEAN",
    prompt: [
      "A check digit is added to the end of an original number. The check digit is the",
      "remainder when the sum of the digits of the original number is divided by 10.",
      "For example, 4162 has digit sum 13, so the new number is 41623.",
      "",
      "A function `CheckNumber()` takes an integer value that already includes its check",
      "digit. It returns `TRUE` if the check digit is correct, otherwise returns `FALSE`.",
      "",
      "For example, 41623 returns `TRUE` and 41633 returns `FALSE`.",
      "Assume that the parameter is valid.",
      "",
      "Write pseudocode for `CheckNumber()`."
    ].join("\n"),
    model: `FUNCTION CheckNumber(Number : INTEGER) RETURNS BOOLEAN
    DECLARE Total : INTEGER
    DECLARE CheckDigit : INTEGER
    DECLARE Rest : INTEGER
    Total <- 0
    CheckDigit <- Number MOD 10
    Rest <- Number DIV 10
    WHILE Rest > 0
        Total <- Total + (Rest MOD 10)
        Rest <- Rest DIV 10
    ENDWHILE
    IF Total MOD 10 = CheckDigit THEN
        RETURN TRUE
    ELSE
        RETURN FALSE
    ENDIF
ENDFUNCTION`,
    after: `OUTPUT CheckNumber(41623)`,
    cases: [
      { label: "CheckNumber(41623)", after: "OUTPUT CheckNumber(41623)" },
      { label: "CheckNumber(41633)", after: "OUTPUT CheckNumber(41633)" },
      { label: "CheckNumber(1236)", after: "OUTPUT CheckNumber(1236)" },
      { label: "CheckNumber(1234)", after: "OUTPUT CheckNumber(1234)" },
    ],
